+Feature: Todo editing
+  As a user of the todo app
+  I want to edit existing todo titles
+  So that I can correct or update my tasks
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo label activates editing mode
+    Given the app has loaded with no persisted todos
+    And I create a todo titled "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the todo label
+    Then the todo li has the editing class
+    And the edit input is focused
+
+  Scenario: Save edit by pressing Enter
+    Given the app has loaded with no persisted todos
+    And I create a todo titled "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the todo label
+    And I type "Buy organic milk" into the edit input
+    And I press Enter in the edit input
+    Then the editing class is removed from the todo li
+    And the todo label shows "Buy organic milk"
+
+  Scenario: Save edit by blurring the input
+    Given the app has loaded with no persisted todos
+    And I create a todo titled "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the todo label
+    And I type "Buy oat milk" into the edit input
+    And the edit input loses focus
+    Then the editing class is removed from the todo li
+    And the todo label shows "Buy oat milk"
+
+  Scenario: Cancel edit by pressing Escape
+    Given the app has loaded with no persisted todos
+    And I create a todo titled "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the todo label
+    And I type "Buy organic milk" into the edit input
+    And I press Escape in the edit input
+    Then the editing class is removed from the todo li
+    And the todo label shows "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Empty title destroys the todo on save
+    Given the app has loaded with no persisted todos
+    And I create a todo titled "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the todo label
+    And I clear the edit input
+    And I press Enter in the edit input
+    Then the todo list is empty
